      "body": "Continues #37599. GitHub currently rejects reopening the original closed PR; this uses the same updated branch and retains the original discussion as context.\n\n## Motivation\n\nFixes #37097.\n\nWhen exact pretokenized input IDs are restored after HF preprocessing, the processor attention mask can have a different length. The single-sequence GLM-V mRoPE call then raises IndexError. Let the existing helper construct its all-ones mask from the final IDs.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Pass attention_mask=None at the unpadded, single-sequence GLM-V call site.\n- Refresh the processor fixture for current-main video configuration and verify exact mRoPE positions with shorter, longer, and absent processor masks.\n\nSynced with current `main` at `f2b73d4f9b4e64415b8d775b0f811c7801f1728b` on October 15, 2026.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Changed-file pre-commit checks, Python syntax compilation, and diff whitespace checks passed.\n- Isolated CPU source regressions: **3 tests passed**. These execute the exact relevant production definitions and test methods with heavy package imports isolated; they are not a normal package/pytest run.\n- Current-main definitions raised the reported mask-shape IndexError for both stale-length cases; all three refreshed processor cases pass.\n- Normal registered-test collection is blocked in this host environment by incompatible Triton/torchvision dependencies. GPU/model end-to-end validation was not run; no working CUDA device is available.\n\nRegistered test for project CI:\n\n```bash\npython test/registered/unit/multimodal/test_glm4v_processor.py\n```\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo speed benchmark was run. The change is limited to the behavior described above.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed-file formatting and lint checks passed.\n- [x] Focused regression coverage added or refreshed using the current CPU CI conventions.\n- [x] No documentation change is needed for this focused fix.\n- [ ] Registered package-level CI and any required GPU validation are pending.\n\nAI assistance was used for the investigation, implementation, and local validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38691235798](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38691235798)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38691235784](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38691235784)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38691235777](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38691235777)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
