  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Hi @mickqian @JustinTong0323, thank you for your time and help with this area.\n\nFollowing up on #37599, which has been awaiting review for several weeks. GitHub currently rejects reopening it, so this PR continues the same updated branch. I would really appreciate your further guidance on the approach and test coverage. I have now merged current `main` (`f2b73d4f9b`), adapted the regression fixture to the current processor and added exact-position checks for shorter, longer, and absent masks, and kept the change focused on #37097.\n\nThe affected pretokenized multimodal requests still fail during preprocessing with IndexError. A timely review would help restore those requests without changing the processor or mRoPE algorithms. Could you please prioritize reviewing the refreshed patch when feasible, and let me know if you would prefer any scope or implementation changes?\n\nChanged-file pre-commit, syntax, and whitespace checks passed. The isolated CPU source regressions passed (3 tests), with the corresponding current-main failure or missing diagnostic confirmed. These are source-level checks; normal package-level pytest collection is blocked by local dependency incompatibilities, and GPU validation is still pending. CI currently stops at the PR gate because the required `run-ci` label is missing, so the gated test jobs have not run. If the approach looks appropriate, could someone with CI permission enable the label and rerun CI for this head?\n\nThank you again for your guidance and consideration.\n",
